    <briefdescription>
<para>Non-owning view onto a <computeroutput>[length, degree, v1, v2, ..., vn]</computeroutput> packed monomial in some externally managed buffer. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_monom" kindref="compound">Monom</ref></computeroutput> is just a <computeroutput>const int*</computeroutput> cursor; the leading int is the total length (including itself), followed by the degree, then the <computeroutput>n</computeroutput> variable indices that spell out the (non-commutative) word. Indexing and <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_monom_a9cb7b2ad287344fbfc6e0f48afe2d7e0_1a9cb7b2ad287344fbfc6e0f48afe2d7e0" kindref="member">begin()</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_monom_a83d0330247dcd7d494d1cf46695578d0_1a83d0330247dcd7d494d1cf46695578d0" kindref="member">end()</ref></computeroutput> give read-only iteration over the whole packed array. The <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_monom" kindref="compound">Monom</ref></computeroutput> knows nothing about which monoid gave it meaning <mdash/> that lives in <computeroutput><ref refid="class_free_monoid" kindref="compound">FreeMonoid</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="res-moninfo_8hpp_a7bc93e1c6a618d8b5a83f61057c445dd_1a7bc93e1c6a618d8b5a83f61057c445dd" kindref="member">ResMonoid</ref></computeroutput>. Weights (added later) extend the format and are not yet reflected in this header comment. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
